{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790712860,"nonce":"rBPnOk8prAFHJN7Y3SZ97eIDMVc=","title":"Hybrid mode intermittently rejects a joint solver method signature","message":"With the installed Ash 0.1.0 release, ChimpMonk's DrivenArm example can fail in the default hybrid mode with:\n\n    Native dispatch: no signature for 6 arguments with kinds [0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 1] returning kind 0\n\nThe call stack points from World.stepSegment at `joints.prepare(h)` into the joint solver. `JointPool.prepare` invokes methods such as `spherical.prepare(id, dx, dy, dz, h)`, where the receiver and arguments match the six reported kinds. This is an inference from the signature; the trace does not name the exact callee.\n\nReproduce from the sibling ChimpMonk checkout:\n\n    haxe -cp . -cp example/src -main DrivenArm -hl /tmp/chimpmonk-driven-arm.hl\n    ash /tmp/chimpmonk-driven-arm.hl\n\nThe first command succeeds. The second has failed repeatedly with the native-dispatch error, sometimes at the first physics step. `ash --mode jit /tmp/chimpmonk-driven-arm.hl` completes and prints all three arm poses. `ash --mode interp` also completed. Explicit `--mode hybrid` completed once but subsequently failed with the same error, suggesting tier timing may affect the failure. A small isolated method with the same argument types did not reproduce it, so the full DrivenArm program is the current reproducer.\n\nAsh's CLI says plain `ash` selects hybrid mode. This failure prevents recommending the default command in ChimpMonk's reader guide; the temporary guide command uses `--mode jit` without pinning a JIT tier. Investigate hybrid native dispatch or promotion for mixed Int/Float/Single instance-method arguments.","files":null}]}